{% comment %}
  Won Discounts — quantity tiers table (MVP 3). App block, product template only.
  Contracts (docs/plans/2026-09-30-won-discounts-mvp3.md):
  - K5 config: app-data metafield, plain namespace (app-data never uses $app).
  - K1/K3 set: the product metafield's tierRef, else (absent) the global set; a
    tierRef the config does not have ("", "~" included) = no tiers (fail closed).
  - K4 v2 margin ceiling per variant (see "K4 v2" below): the floor `f` of `pdp`,
    a percent ceiling for a variant without a cost, or no table (fail closed).
    A cost is never printed.
  - K6 count: the chosen quantity + cart items counted toward the same tier
    (see the cart pass below); per item the page floors, per line it rounds
    like the engine, so it never shows more than checkout gives.
  - K8 markup, mirrored by the admin preview; styles in won-discounts-tiers.css.
  Liquid renders the selected variant; assets/won-discounts-tiers.js (+ its pure
  logic in won-discounts-tiers-core.js) keeps it live from the JSON at the end.
  Neither changes nor reads the cart (SF-1).
  In the theme editor a table the customer would not see (no set, no amount in the cart's currency, the selected
  variant on sale, under margin protection or a gift card) is followed by a labelled sample of the same markup at
  the product's price, saying why; the real (hidden) table stays as it was for the script.
  Text keys tiers.*: the extension locales; a merchant text in the page's language (metafield tx_<locale>) wins.
{% endcomment %}
{%- comment -%} The table itself: snippets/won-tiers.liquid (the embed renders it for a tag too). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- render 'won-tiers', accent: block.settings.accent, scripts: true -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Quantity tiers",
  "target": "section",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "stylesheet": "won-discounts-tiers.css",
  "javascript": "won-discounts-tiers.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent",
      "label": "Accent color",
      "info": "Highlights the tier the shopper reaches. Empty = the theme's text color."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
